  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Use the quadratic formula, or by completing the square, find the solutions $\\alpha,\\beta$ of each equation, then rewrite each equation in factored form $a(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)=0$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-6x+4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=3-\\sqrt5$, $\\beta=3+\\sqrt5$.\n\n$(x-3+\\sqrt5)(x-3-\\sqrt5)=0$.",
          "worked": "$a=1$, $b=-6$, $c=4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(1)(4)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{20}}2\\\\x&=3\\pm\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\alpha=3-\\sqrt5$ and $\\beta=3+\\sqrt5$. The factored equation is\n\n$$(x-3+\\sqrt5)(x-3-\\sqrt5)=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2-3x+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt5}{2}$, $\\beta=\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}$.\n\n$\\left(x-\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)\\left(x-\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)=0$.",
          "worked": "$a=1$, $b=-3$, $c=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-3)\\pm\\sqrt{(-3)^2-4(1)(1)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\alpha=\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt5}{2}$ and $\\beta=\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}$. The factored equation is\n\n$$\\left(x-\\frac{3-\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3x^2+6x+2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=\\dfrac{-3-\\sqrt3}{3}$, $\\beta=\\dfrac{-3+\\sqrt3}{3}$.\n\n$3\\left(x+\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt3}{3}\\right)\\left(x+\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt3}{3}\\right)=0$.",
          "worked": "$a=3$, $b=6$, $c=2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{6^2-4(3)(2)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{12}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt3}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\alpha=\\dfrac{-3-\\sqrt3}{3}$ and $\\beta=\\dfrac{-3+\\sqrt3}{3}$. Retaining the leading coefficient, the factored equation is\n\n$$3\\left(x+\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}{3}\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{3-\\sqrt3}{3}\\right)=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 88
      }
    ]
  },
